# OkVevo stays on upstream Hermes

**Product pivot:** the shipped product is the **OkVevo** desktop app (Mac/Windows) plus the **OkVevo-Web** portal. **Nia** is the retired name — never in user-facing text or new names. Keep internal ids: `~/.hermes`, `hermes` CLI, `@hermes` protocol handle, repo slug `OkVevo-Nia`.

The desktop app does not call a paid or AI vendor itself. Chat, images, video, and web search go through the OkVevo portal. Allowed hosts: `docs/okvevo/VENDOR-TOUCHPOINTS.md`.

First-run values live in `okvevo/config/okvevo-defaults.yaml`. Do not copy them into TypeScript.

Do not edit upstream Python (`gateway/`, `agent/`, `hermes_cli/`, `providers/`) to make an OkVevo check pass. If a check fails, fix the OkVevo-owned path or rebuild the app the way upstream packs it.

Push only the `okvevo` remote. Never `origin`. Land changes via **PRs** (see `okvevo-remote.mdc` / `okvevo-cicd.mdc`).

## OkVevo-owned surface (must survive every upstream sync)

Every OkVevo change (features, branding, icons, `@okvevo` display alias, About, UI) lives in:

- **OkVevo-owned files** (`brand/`, `okvevo/`, `plugins/okvevo/`, `docs/okvevo/`, pack scripts under `apps/desktop/scripts/` that are OkVevo-specific), or
- **overrides**, or
- **tiny listed hooks** in upstream files (one-line re-apply / brand path) recorded in `docs/okvevo/PATCHES.md`.

Canonical ledgers (read these — **not** `docs/fork-deltas/`):

| Doc | Job |
|-----|-----|
| `docs/okvevo/PATCHES.md` | Upstream touch list + keep reasons |
| `docs/okvevo/WORKAROUNDS.md` | Temporary behavior toggles |
| `docs/okvevo/UI-CONTRACT.md` | Design tokens + element rows + baselines |
| `docs/okvevo/SYNC.md` | Sync procedure |
| `docs/okvevo/NOUS-TOUCHPOINTS.md` | Allowed Nous host hits |
| `docs/okvevo/VENDOR-TOUCHPOINTS.md` | Allowed vendor hosts |
| `/okvevo-sync` (`.cursor/commands/okvevo-sync.md`) | Agent sync checklist |

Brand assets live under `brand/` (`brand/assets/`, `brand/locales/`). Pack and locale load apply them — do not commit replacement icon blobs onto upstream paths. **`brand/nia.json` is a deferred rename** to `brand/okvevo.json` (later code PR); do not invent a second brand catalog until that lands.

Keep `LICENSE` / NOTICE / copyright attribution. Never strip Hermes attribution. Never rename wire/internal Hermes identifiers for fun.

## Upstream syncs (same rules as `docs/okvevo/SYNC.md`)

- Sync every Hermes release, and at least every 2 weeks when no tag landed.
- `git merge` the tag; never rebase OkVevo onto it. `git config rerere.enabled true` on the merging clone (not CI).
- One sync per **PR into `staging`**. Never start a sync inside a feature PR. Never blind-merge `origin/main`.
- Do not treat Hermes Cloud / Nous billing / Skills Hub Nous origin as OkVevo product.

### Guards that must pass on every sync PR

Merge only when green:

1. OkVevo parity + desktop E2E suite (including packed `@okvevo` E2E)
2. `python3 scripts/okvevo/check_branding.py`
3. Identity tests (product identity / About / no user-facing “Nia” regressions as covered by the suite)
4. Icon artifact check (`ci-assert-packaged-icons` / packaged icon hashes)
5. UI-CONTRACT visual baselines (per-OS; `--update-snapshots` in the same PR when UI changes)
6. Nous-diff scan vs `NOUS-TOUCHPOINTS.md`
7. `python3 scripts/okvevo/check_vendor_keys.py` + vendor-host guard

Every sync also reads `docs/okvevo/UPSTREAM-KNOWN-ISSUES.md` and `WORKAROUNDS.md`, runs each workaround’s behavior test with its toggle off, and recommends removal when Hermes passes. Karan decides.

## UI contract (syncs and OkVevo UI changes)

Follow `docs/okvevo/UI-CONTRACT.md` and `docs/okvevo/SYNC.md`:

1. Use design tokens (no hard-coded colors/fonts). Styling contracts live in tokens + `UI-CONTRACT.md` — not a separate Cursor styling rule.
2. Prefer OkVevo-owned files or overrides; upstream edits go in `PATCHES.md` with a reason.
3. Add or update the element row in `UI-CONTRACT.md`.
4. Update per-OS screenshot baselines in the same PR; show the diff for approval.

## Icon / BrandMark pack clash rule

On conflict in `before-build.mjs`, `after-pack.mjs`, `set-exe-identity.mjs`, `electron-builder.config.cjs` (NSIS/DMG icons), or `brand-mark.tsx`: take upstream, re-apply the OkVevo one-line hook / brand path (`okvevo-brand-paths.mjs`, `overlayBrandAssets`). Every sync PR must pass the icon artifact check, packed `@okvevo` E2E, About-version stamp, and UI-CONTRACT baselines before merge.
